-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Dakin</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Yuan</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Sierks</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>McGowan</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Reed</surname><given-names>DK</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenberry</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name><name><surname>Das</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Golde</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Insights into the mechanisms of action of anti-Abeta antibodies in Alzheimer's disease mouse models</article-title><source>Faseb J</source><year>2006</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>2576</fpage><lpage>2578</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17068112</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1096/fj.06-6463fje</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Griffin</surname><given-names>WS</given-names></name><name><surname>Stanley</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Ling</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>MacLeod</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Perrot</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>CL</given-names><suffix>3rd</suffix></name><name><surname>Araoz</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Brain interleukin 1 and S-100 immunoreactivity are elevated in Down syndrome and Alzheimer disease</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><year>1989</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>7611</fpage><lpage>7615</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2529544</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.86.19.7611</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mrak</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Griffin</surname><given-names>WS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Common inflammatory mechanisms in Lewy body disease and Alzheimer disease</article-title><source>J Neuropathol Exp Neurol</source><year>2007</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>683</fpage><lpage>686</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17882012</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>